From: dotlouis <1891109+dotlouis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:04:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/41] MTROPOLIS: Support the objectid attribute

Scripts can read "objectid", a number that identifies an object while
the project runs. Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage uses it to tell the
toads apart in the sorcerer's hut, and failed with "Unable to read
object attribute 'objectid'".

Return the runtime GUID of the object.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp b/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp
index 052c9b02e8a..2385eb72b08 100644
--- a/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp
+++ b/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp
@@ -2868,6 +2868,13 @@ bool RuntimeObject::isElement() const {
 }
 
 bool RuntimeObject::readAttribute(MiniscriptThread *thread, DynamicValue &result, const Common::String &attrib) {
+	// A number that identifies the object while the project runs. Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage uses it to tell
+	// toads apart in the sorcerer's hut.
+	if (attrib == "objectid") {
+		result.setInt(static_cast<int32>(_runtimeGUID));
+		return true;
+	}
+
 	return false;
 }
 
